     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I used to be able to plot a map of the world on ggplot 2 by first &quot;fortifying&quot; the shapefile with the following command:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div> FAO_fort &lt;- fortify(FAO, region=&quot;id&quot;)# fortify to plot with ggplot2</div><div>Error in function (classes, fdef, mtable)  : </div><div>  unable to find an inherited method for function &quot;proj4string&quot;, for signature &quot;NULL&quot; </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>However for some reason, I now get this error message and I can&#39;t figure out what is the problem.</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; str(FAO,max.level=2)</div><div>Formal class &#39;SpatialPolygonsDataFrame&#39; [package &quot;sp&quot;] with 5 slots</div><div>  ..@ data       :&#39;data.frame&#39;:<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>19 obs. of  2 variables:</div><div>  ..@ polygons   :List of 19</div><div>  ..@ plotOrder  : int [1:19] 18 2 17 4 12 3 13 11 5 6 ...</div><div>  ..@ bbox       : num [1:2, 1:2] -180 -85.5 180 90</div><div>  .. ..- attr(*, &quot;dimnames&quot;)=List of 2</div><div>  ..@ proj4string:Formal class &#39;CRS&#39; [package &quot;sp&quot;] with 1 slots</div></div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; FAO@proj4string</div><div>CRS arguments:</div><div> +proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs +ellps=WGS84 +towgs84=0,0,0 </div></div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be appreciated!</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div></div><div><br></div><div>Aurelie</div><br><br><div>\r\n<span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Century Gothic&#39;;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Century Gothic&#39;;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:nor